-- title:
--   Lemma 3.3 — calibration by single-vertex updates stops within $\lceil 2n/\rho^2\rceil$ updates
-- statement:
--   Let $G(\omega)$ be the random subgraph of a finite simple graph $G=(V,E)$, $n=|V|$, with independent edges of probabilities $q_e\in[0,1]$; let $\mathcal A$ be a randomized matching algorithm and $s_v=\mathbb E X_v$ the marginals of $M=\mathcal A(G(\omega))$; let $m_v(\theta)$ be the marginals of the perturbed optimum $M^\theta$. Let $\rho\in(0,1)$. Start with $\theta=0$. Whenever $|s_v-m_v(\theta)|>\rho$ for some vertex $v$, make the update
--
--   $$h:=s_v-m_v(\theta),\qquad \theta_v\leftarrow\theta_v+h,$$
--
--   leaving all other offsets unchanged, the violating vertex being chosen by a fixed deterministic rule. Then after at most $\lceil 2n/\rho^2\rceil$ updates the process stops at a vector $\theta^{(\rho)}$ satisfying
--
--   $$\max_v|m_v(\theta^{(\rho)})-s_v|\le\rho,\qquad \|\theta^{(\rho)}\|_\infty\le\frac{2n}{\rho}.$$
--
--   This is the calibration step of Lemma 3.1: perturbed weight maximization can match any feasible marginal vector up to $\rho$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: X^θ_v = 1{v ∈ V(M^θ)} for the matching M^θ maximizing the covered-vertex weight, unique almost surely → coverIndicator S (θ + ξ) v = 1 iff some matching of S covering v scores strictly more than every matching of S not covering v; reason: the two agree whenever θ + ξ is generic, which holds outside a null set of ties; expectations are unchanged
--   - encoding: a fixed deterministic rule for choosing a violating vertex → any sequence θ 0 = 0, θ 1, … that at each step applies update (8) to some violating vertex if one exists and otherwise stays put; reason: every deterministic rule (also a history-dependent one) generates such a sequence, and each such sequence is generated by the rule that follows it
--   - encoding: the §3.3 standing assumption: s_v = E X_v for M = A(G(ω)), A a randomized matching algorithm → hypotheses IsRandMatching G.edgeFinset π and s = marg q G.edgeFinset π; reason: trap 19: the section's assumption is a binder; no instance changes
--   - encoding: a finite graph G (the setting of Lemma 3.1, §3) → a finite simple graph (SimpleGraph on a Fintype V); reason: §4.1: all graphs in the main argument are finite, undirected and simple; a matching uses no loop and parallel copies of an edge cover the same vertices, so the covered-set statements do not change
-- source:
--   S. Behnezhad, Stochastic Matching with Polynomial Degree, arXiv:2611.03367 (preprint, held version, sha256 409beb43bd8ab862a4a4a595be9c08afd92590790382102cb640d81d9b564017), Lemma 3.3, p.7 (PDF p.8); §3.3 preamble, p.7

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_StochMatchPoly_edgeLaw
import Definitions.Def_StochMatchPoly_IsRandMatching
import Definitions.Def_StochMatchPoly_perturbedCover

open Classical

namespace StochMatchPoly

/-- S. Behnezhad, *Stochastic Matching with Polynomial Degree*, arXiv:2611.03367 (held version,
sha256 409beb43…), Lemma 3.3 (Calibration by single-vertex updates), p.7 (PDF p.8), with the
setting of §3.3, p.7.

"Let ρ ∈ (0, 1). Start with θ = 0. Whenever |s_v − m_v(θ)| > ρ for some vertex v, make the update
h := s_v − m_v(θ), θ_v ← θ_v + h, (8) leaving all other offsets unchanged. Fix a deterministic rule
for choosing a violating vertex. After at most ⌈2n/ρ²⌉ updates, the process stops at a
deterministic vector θ^(ρ) satisfying max_v |m_v(θ^(ρ)) − s_v| ≤ ρ, ‖θ^(ρ)‖_∞ ≤ 2n/ρ. (9)"

**Formalization Note.** The §3.3 setting: `s_v = E X_v` for the coverage vector `X` of
`M = A(G(ω))`, `A` a randomized matching algorithm (kernel `π`), under independent edges with
probabilities `q e ∈ [0, 1]`; `n = |V|`. The process is any sequence `θ 0 = 0, θ 1, …` in which
each step updates, by (8), some violating vertex when one exists, and stays put otherwise; every
deterministic choice rule (also one that depends on the history) produces such a sequence. The
conclusion gives the number `K` of updates (`θ k` has a violator exactly for `k < K`), the
bound `K ≤ ⌈2n/ρ²⌉` of the statement, and (9) at `θ^(ρ) = θ K`. -/
theorem lemma_3_3 {V : Type*} [Fintype V] (G : SimpleGraph V) (q : Sym2 V → ℝ)
    (hq : ∀ e ∈ G.edgeFinset, 0 ≤ q e ∧ q e ≤ 1)
    (π : Finset (Sym2 V) → Finset (Sym2 V) → ℝ) (hπ : IsRandMatching G.edgeFinset π)
    (s : V → ℝ) (hs : s = marg q G.edgeFinset π) (ρ : ℝ) (hρ0 : 0 < ρ) (hρ1 : ρ < 1)
    (θ : ℕ → V → ℝ) (h0 : θ 0 = 0)
    (hstep : ∀ k,
      ((∃ v, ρ < |s v - mθ q G.edgeFinset (θ k) v|) →
        ∃ v, ρ < |s v - mθ q G.edgeFinset (θ k) v| ∧
          θ (k + 1) = Function.update (θ k) v (θ k v + (s v - mθ q G.edgeFinset (θ k) v))) ∧
      ((¬ ∃ v, ρ < |s v - mθ q G.edgeFinset (θ k) v|) → θ (k + 1) = θ k)) :
    ∃ K : ℕ, K ≤ ⌈2 * (Fintype.card V : ℝ) / ρ ^ 2⌉₊ ∧
      (∀ k < K, ∃ v, ρ < |s v - mθ q G.edgeFinset (θ k) v|) ∧
      (∀ v, |mθ q G.edgeFinset (θ K) v - s v| ≤ ρ) ∧
      ∀ v, |θ K v| ≤ 2 * (Fintype.card V : ℝ) / ρ := by sorry

end StochMatchPoly
